Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Adreno 220 ("Adreno (TM) 220") is an Adreno 2xx for the sub-texture upload workaround
(glTexSubImage2D into a big texture is 16 times slower than a whole glTexImage2D on it). An EGL
context prefers BGRA for 32-bit surfaces where GL_EXT_texture_format_BGRA8888 is present, with
the GLES-legal type and internal format (an RGBA upload of a 768x942 layer costs 35 ms, a BGRA
one 8; as RGBA the CPU swizzled every tile first). GLContextEGL::JihadCreateSharedContext makes
a 1x1 pbuffer context sharing a compositor context's objects, for a readback thread. Opt-in and
measured as no gain: a fresh texture name per upload with the retired names deleted once the GPU
is idle (JIHAD_GPU_FRESH_TEX=1; the driver waits for pending GPU work on any upload).
